# Local Provider Endpoint UI

When editing the local-deployment provider in Settings (brand === 'local'),
the endpoint list is rendered as **structured rows**, not a plain textarea.
Each row = status light + URL `<input>` + per-row test (`↻`) + per-row
delete (`✕`) buttons. Above the list is a toolbar with: + 添加端点,
📝 批量编辑 (opens a paste-many modal), 🔍 探测全部, 🗑 清空.

Key files & functions in `static/js/settings.js`:
- `addLocalProvider()` — bootstraps a fresh `endpoints: ['']` row
- `_renderLocalEndpointsSection(provIdx, list)` — renders the field block
- `_renderLocalEndpointRow(provIdx, epIdx, url)` — single row
- `_localEndpointStatus[url]` — in-memory probe-status cache
  (`{ok, status: 'ok'|'error'|'pending'|'unknown', message, ts, n_models}`)
- `_probeLocalEndpoint(provIdx, epIdx)` — single-row probe via
  POST `/api/provider-probe-bulk` with one URL
- `_discoverLocalModels(provIdx)` — bulk probe, also populates the cache
- `_refreshLocalEndpointRow` — in-place DOM update so blurring an
  input doesn't kill focus mid-edit
- `_localEndpointBadge(urls)` — builds the header badge with an
  aggregated dot (ok/error/mixed/unknown)

CSS is under `Local Endpoint Rows` section in `static/styles.css`
(class prefix `stg-ep-*`). Status lights use 4 classes:
`ok` (green), `error` (red), `pending` (amber, animated),
`unknown` (gray).

Storage shape on disk (provider entry in `data/config/server_config.json`):
```
{ "brand": "local", "endpoints": ["http://a/v1", "http://b/v1"], ... }
```
The `base_url` field is auto-synced to `endpoints[0]` for legacy
code paths (balance URL, dispatcher fallback).

